# Agent workflow

Full workflow: [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md). This rule covers mandatory **task start** behaviour.

## New task (mandatory first steps)

When the user asks for the next task, to pick up work, or to start a new issue:

1. **First action:** call `SwitchMode` with `target_mode_id: plan`.
2. **Second action (same turn, before research):** if a GitHub issue applies, move it to **Planning** on the dosmud project board. Required even in plan mode - this is workflow metadata, not implementation. Never defer until plan approval.
3. Stay in plan mode until the user confirms the plan or explicitly asks to execute (e.g. "go ahead", "implement", "execute the plan").
4. In plan mode: gather context and produce a plan only. No repo file edits, branches, builds, or code changes.

### Allowed in plan mode (workflow only)

- GitHub project status transitions (Planning, In progress, Review)
- Posting implementation plan comments on the linked issue
- Read-only exploration (`gh issue view`, reading files, `git log`)
- Milestone issue hygiene **GitHub-only** (project #1 Size/Priority, blocked-by, issue body, stack order, hygiene comment) per [milestone-issue-hygiene](../skills/milestone-issue-hygiene/SKILL.md) when creating or grooming roadmap issues — **not** `DEV_PLAN.md` file commits (those belong in a docs or implementation PR after plan mode)

### Not allowed in plan mode

- Branch creation, code edits, commits, PRs
- `make build`, `make test`, or other commands that change repo artifacts

## Before implementation

- Confirm an open issue exists; never modify closed issues.
- Post agreed implementation details as an issue comment, then move **Planning** to **In progress**.
- Implementation plan or issue comment must include a **Testing** subsection (`Unit:` / `Snapshots:` lines or "none - reason"). See [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md) Planning expectations and [`docs/testing.md`](../../docs/testing.md#when-to-add-or-update-tests).
- Create a branch before any code changes.
- Prefer the top **Agent-ready** issue when the user asks for the next task.

## Before opening a PR

- Update [`DEV_PLAN.md`](../../DEV_PLAN.md) per **DEV_PLAN updates** in [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md) when opening the draft PR.
- Run `make test`, `make test-run`, and `make test-unit` (or `make test-all`).
- Follow [When to add or update tests](../../docs/testing.md#when-to-add-or-update-tests); if in-scope `src/*.c` gained or changed **exported** gameplay APIs (module `.h`), update matching `tests/unit/unit_*.c` or explain why not in the PR **Test plan**.
- PR body **Test plan** lists new or updated tests (not only "all green").
- Open a **draft** PR linked to the issue; move project status to **Review**.
- Match PR labels to the issue; follow PR title/commit rules in `AGENTS.md` and [commit-messages.mdc](commit-messages.mdc).

## After pushing to an open PR (mandatory)

See [`.cursor/rules/pr-after-push.mdc`](pr-after-push.mdc) and [`.cursor/skills/pr-after-push/SKILL.md`](../skills/pr-after-push/SKILL.md). Complete that gate in the **same turn** as `git push` before the user-facing summary.

### PR push checklist (complete before replying)

- [ ] `git push` succeeded
- [ ] Open PR exists for this branch
- [ ] Post-push gate completed ([`pr-after-push.mdc`](pr-after-push.mdc))
- [ ] Only then: user-facing summary
